    "notes": [
      "The binary profile uses x86-64 baseline/SSE2, with AVX2/AVX512/NEON/SVE/SVE2 disabled. Header consumers may choose their own SIMD flags; this is not cross-CPU/OS qualification.",
      "CMake and Ninja are build-only prerequisites. Matching pinned system installations are the default; the maintainer replay can explicitly bind private copies extracted from the same locked Ubuntu debs without changing the APT database.",
      "Do not divide by zero. Unsigned branchfree dividers do not accept denominator 1. Signed INT_MIN / -1 is not a representable quotient and is excluded from C/C++ division comparisons.",
      "The original source-selector and target contract is preserved in metadata.catalog. Canonical checks only need headers, source and test executables already present in the original source installation.",
      "Upstream test_c99 reports arithmetic discrepancies to stderr without returning failure; the check treats its Division fail diagnostic as failure. Benchmarks are provided as upstream tools, not a framework official Benchmark result."
    ],
